# Round sparkr3 (kind profile: no A/B, no ruler). The one term of the Spark tier plan only the cable and the
# Spark can fix: a, the exposed tier round trip a layer inside the engine, from the go leaving node 0 until the
# tier rows are readable by its card.
# Source: sparktier report 4.2 (a_sum in [110, 170] [derived]: go one way ~26 us = half the 8 KiB RTT 50-53 us,
# the compact reply ~34 us one way, node-side chain floor 25-60 us [assumption], pump/poll hops 15-40 us
# [assumption]; a compact reply adds ~10 us over a summed row) and 8; the R0 result (rig-log
# log/2026-11-04.md#sparkr0-wc: wc = 150.7 prose / 167.1 code us a layer) tightened the bar [derived, the
# sparktier 4.3 model rerun at the measured wc]: break-even a = 197-198 us prose, 173-178 us code; at a = 140
# prose +5.2..+7.2 %, code +2.4..+2.9 %; at a = 170 prose +2.8..+3.7 %, code +0.4..+1.1 % (inside the six-round
# ruler, +-0.8 %).
# Link facts: 10GbE direct, MTU 1500, busy-poll both ends, the Spark's shallow-idle unit up for the run
# (rig-log log/2026-11-04.md#spark-wire-tuning: 8 KiB p50 50.2 us, p99 116.4; 16 KiB p50 67.0).
kind: profile
question: what is a, the exposed per-layer tier round trip of a V4.1 decode step with the Spark as the expert
  tier node over the TCP wire, and does it land at or below the 140 us at which both corpora's decode gain is
  claimable at six rounds?
term: a, us a layer, mean over layers 2..39 and the timed replays: from the go frame leaving the host pump
  until the layer's join sees the tier rows (the tier done word), one value per arm, prose and code, decode
  depth 512 (the first 512 ids of corpus-prose.ids and corpus-code.ids, n 8, 7 replays), the compact reply,
  BLOOMERY_TIER_LINK=tcp, the ws's cards as plan (a) and the Spark holding the tier image
unit: us
predict: 110..175
condition: the r1wire and r2compact changes landed, the tier_server built natively on the Spark from the same
  commit (rig-log tools/bloomery-follow/spark-box.sh), cpuidle-shallow started on the Spark for the run and
  stopped after; one lease on the A6000; the witness shows no [other-busy] or [cpu-busy] and a warm file
  (pgmajfault unmoved between the pre and post witness); the per-layer a is read from the step's profile
  records (BLOOMERY_PROFILE=1, the tier leg's go and join stamps), its cross-check the link_probe --tcp RTT
  table on the cable taken in the same sitting (8 KiB p50 within 50..60 us, else the link, not the engine,
  moved)
decide-in: at or below 140: open the same-lease decode A/B card (ws alone vs ws+Spark, prose and code at depth
  512, six rounds, an A/A arm; the predicted effect from the model rerun at the measured a and wc); between
  140 and 175: the prose A/B only, the code rows need 13 rounds (+-0.5 %) and are not opened tonight
decide-below: less than 110: the chain floor and hop assumptions were high: rerun the model at the measured a,
  write the larger predicted effect into the A/B card, and open both corpora
decide-above: above 175: the decode plan at Q3_K_M stops (code negative, prose inside the ruler above 198);
  read where the time goes (pump hop, node-side H2D/D2H, the wire's ack) before any A/B; the capacity regime
  (Q4_K_M, R5) stays open and does not depend on a
